# ScribeShade: AI Answer Lifecycle & Context Architecture
**Technical Specification & Optimization Blueprint**  
*Document Version: 1.4.0*  
*Author: Senior AI Systems Architect*

---

## 1. Executive Summary

ScribeShade is a desktop-first productivity application designed to provide real-time interview coaching, screen analysis, and resume/project tailoring. This document details the lifecycle of the AI-powered answering system, analyzing how context is gathered, processed, and transmitted to LLMs via OpenRouter. 

The current system relies on a monolithic context assembly pipeline that transmits up to **15,000+ tokens** on every single user request. This document exposes key structural bottlenecks—specifically payload bloat, redundant historical context injection, and sequential vector embeddings—and presents a concrete, implementable blueprint for a **Context Intelligence Engine (CIE)**. The CIE introduces rolling transcript memory, semantic context pruning, and token budgeting, aiming to reduce latency by **40%** and API token costs by **65%** while preserving output relevance.

---

## 2. Current Architecture Overview

The system bridges a high-performance Tauri desktop app (Rust + React) with a TypeScript/Express backend, orchestrating audio capture, transcription, semantic retrieval, and streaming LLM inference.

### High-Level System Architecture

```mermaid
graph TD
    %% Frontend Components
    subgraph Frontend [Tauri Desktop Client]
        Launcher["Launcher Widget (WidgetApp.tsx)"]
        Overlay["Mini Transcription Overlay (FloatingApp.tsx)"]
        useNative["useNativeTabTranscription Hook"]
        useAIChat["useAIChat Hook (Vite React)"]
    end

    %% OS & Third Party
    subgraph AudioCapture [OS Loopback]
        SCKit["ScreenCaptureKit (macOS 13.0+)"]
    end
    
    subgraph ThirdParty [Third-Party Services]
        DG["Deepgram WebSocket API"]
        OR["OpenRouter API Gateway"]
    end

    %% Backend Services
    subgraph Backend [ScribeShade Express Backend]
        Router["Session Router (session.router.ts)"]
        Controller["Session Controller (session.controller.ts)"]
        Service["Session Service (session.service.ts)"]
        RAG["RAG Service (rag.service.ts)"]
        Embed["Embedding Service (embedding.service.ts)"]
        PrismaDB[("PostgreSQL DB (Prisma + pgvector)")]
    end

    %% Flow Connections
    SCKit -->|Raw Float32 PCM| Launcher
    Launcher -->|axum WS / i16 PCM| useNative
    useNative -->|PCM linear16| DG
    DG -->|Live Text Chunks| useNative
    useNative -->|Local Transcript State| useAIChat
    
    useAIChat -->|POST /api/session/:id/ai-answer| Router
    Router --> Controller
    Controller --> Service
    Service -->|Query| RAG
    RAG -->|Generate Query Vector| Embed
    Embed -->|REST POST /embeddings| OR
    OR -->|2560-dim Array| Embed
    Embed -->|Query vector distance < 0.6| PrismaDB
    PrismaDB -->|Semantic Chunk Excerpts| Service
    Service -->|Combined System + User Prompts| OR
    OR -->|Inference Stream (Gemini 2.0 / Fallback)| Service
    Service -->|Chunked Response Text| Controller
    Controller -->|res.write Chunk Stream| useAIChat
```

