## 5. AI Answer Button Lifecycle

The user interacts with the transcription stream via two trigger actions: clicking the **AI Answer** button (transcribed voice) or **Analyze Screen** (visual screenshot OCR). Both trigger streaming execution pipelines.

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant UI as useAIChat Hook (Frontend)
    participant API as Session Controller (Backend)
    participant Serv as Session Service
    participant DB as Prisma (PostgreSQL)
    participant OR as OpenRouter API

    UI->>API: POST /api/session/:id/ai-answer { transcript: "...", aiModel: "..." }
    Note over UI,API: Request isolates and cancels prior running streams

    activate API
    API->>Serv: getAIAnswer(id, transcript, isCustomQuery, isRegenerate, model)
    activate Serv
    
    Serv->>DB: Fetch Session details, JD, and ResumeId
    Serv->>Serv: Build RAG Query & Fetch context
    
    Serv->>DB: Query semantically matching TranscriptChunks
    DB-->>Serv: Return topK matches (distance < 0.6)
    
    Serv->>Serv: Construct System Prompt (Rules 0-8) & User Message
    
    Serv->>OR: Call Model Stream (Gemini 2.0 / GPT-4o)
    activate OR
    OR-->>Serv: SSE Text stream chunks
    deactivate OR

    Loop Stream Translation
        Serv-->>API: Yield delta text tokens
        API-->>UI: Write raw text chunk (res.write)
        Note over UI: useAIChat splits stream on ===NEXT_QUESTION===
    end

    deactivate Serv
    API-->>UI: Close connection (res.end)
    deactivate API

    Note over Serv,DB: Post-Processing Loop (Runs Asynchronously)
    Serv->>Serv: Parse final response into Q&A blocks
    Serv->>DB: Write to QA Table & append to messages JSON
```

