## 17. Estimated Cost Reduction

Implementing the CIE, token budgeting, and caching strategies is estimated to significantly reduce operating costs.

### Cost Comparison (1,000 Sessions, ~40 requests/session)

```mermaid
gantt
    title Token Footprint Optimization
    dateFormat  X
    axisFormat %s
    
    section Monolithic Context (Old)
    Input Tokens (15k/req)   :active, 0, 15000
    
    section Optimized Context (New)
    CIE Budgeted (4k/req)    :done, 0, 4000
```

| Parameter | Monolithic Context (Current) | Budgeted Context (CIE) | Projected Savings |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Avg. Input Tokens / Request** | 14,850 tokens | 4,000 tokens | **-73.0%** |
| **Input Cost / Request (Gemini)** | $0.00111 | $0.00030 | **-73.0%** |
| **Avg. Output Tokens / Request** | 450 tokens | 400 tokens | -11.1% |
| **Output Cost / Request** | $0.000135 | $0.000120 | -11.1% |
| **Total Cost / Session (40 reqs)** | **$0.0498** | **$0.0168** | **-66.2%** |
| **Monthly Cost / 1,000 Active Users** | **$498.00** | **$168.00** | **Save $330.00/mo** |
| **Average Stream Start Latency** | 1.8 seconds | 0.9 seconds | **-50.0%** |

---

## 18. Final Recommended Production Architecture

To implement the Context Intelligence Engine (CIE) while maintaining backward compatibility, we recommend a modular, service-based refactoring plan.

```mermaid
graph TD
    %% Controllers and Routers
    Router["session.router.ts"] --> Controller["session.controller.ts"]
    
    %% CIE Core System
    Controller --> CIE["cie.service.ts
    (Context Intelligence Engine)"]
    
    %% CIE Sub-Components
    CIE --> Classifier["Query Classifier
    (Route request type)"]
    CIE --> Budgeter["Token Budgeter
    (Enforce 4k limits)"]
    CIE --> Cache["Context Cache Manager
    (Redis Storage Gateway)"]
    
    %% Supporting Services
    Classifier --> RAG["rag.service.ts
    (Parallelized vector fetching)"]
    Classifier --> Memory["memory.service.ts
    (Adaptive sliding window history)"]
    
    %% Target Execution
    Budgeter --> TargetModel["OpenRouter Client Dispatcher"]
```

### Key Implementation Milestones

1. **Develop the CIE Service (`src/features/session/cie.service.ts`)**:
   - Centralize context assembly logic.
   - Implement query classification using pattern matching to identify conceptual, behavioral, or technical requests.
   
2. **Implement Token Budgeting & Truncation**:
   - Integrate a lightweight token estimator (e.g., `js-tiktoken`).
   - Implement dynamic truncation for resumes, supporting documents, and projects when the context size exceeds the token budget.
   - Set up strict limits: Resumes capped at 1,000 tokens, supporting docs at 400 tokens, projects at 800 tokens, sliding history window at 600 tokens.

3. **Upgrade the RAG Service**:
   - Refactor the database query logic to use parallel execution paths (`Promise.all`).
   - Move post-session transcript indexing and vector generation tasks to asynchronous background jobs.

4. **Integrate Redis Caching**:
   - Cache static session context (resumes, projects) in Redis to minimize database load.
   - Cache query embeddings to prevent duplicate processing.
